  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6208113063863868999}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Basic control of these areas are given to the \u201CAdmins\u201D of the
    area. What can admins control? \n\nWhat you see, hear, feel, smell, even down
    to words being filtered as you speak them. They can even shut down their \u2018server\u2019
    and end up booting everyone.\n\nInstead of \u2018world\u2019, \u2018shards\u2019,
    or \u2018servers\u2019 ( they sound so lame and outdated ) , users adopted the
    name \u2018domain.\u2019\n\nThe only ones that can authorize a person into a
    \u2018domain\u2019 are the admins and the primary moderators. These key roles
    are given from the owner, who is normally the company that owns the servers. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9476861b6a9cdca409e8769907d1a9d0, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 9137770337806101678, guid: 9476861b6a9cdca409e8769907d1a9d0,
    type: 2}
